{
  "title": "About Skins Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "bf959d214937c934",
      "text": "This page is a [[Stub]] generated through a dialogue between [[David Bovill]] and [[Claude Code]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "591a2413afa87d94",
      "text": "The Skins plugin is the [[Skin Switcher]]. The page is the truth; the skin is a lens. Every skin reads the same lineup of page-json and draws it its own way, and the \"Skin\" dropdown in the footer switches between them while keeping the same pages in view."
    },
    {
      "type": "skins",
      "id": "f50ecf6f7c92c512",
      "text": "Show this lineup in another skin:"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "26ce22347daf641b",
      "text": "# What it ships\n> Three files every skin leans on."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "f53c6dfb1793b5c8",
      "text": "- **skin-kit.js** \u2014 the [[Skin Contract]] in code: Read the lineup and its pages, Render items, Return changes as journaled actions.\n- **The Skin dropdown** \u2014 added to the classic footer on every page.\n- **Wear** \u2014 hosts a guest skin in a sandbox; it can read but must ask before changing a page."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "132d00b531cbb2f3",
      "text": "# Making a skin\n> A plugin named skin-something with two files."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "6096f4d6cfe3344c",
      "text": "A skin is a plugin called `wiki-plugin-skin-<id>` whose client folder holds `skin.html` and `skin.json`. See [[Vibe Coding a Skin]] and the [[Triptych Skin]] for a worked example."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "6938abd955b7eb06",
      "text": "# See\n- [[Same Page, Many Skins]]\n- [[Skin Kit]]\n- [[Trusted and Guest Skins]]"
    }
  ],
